From 878850f94dab7b5efb9c7722d013969a02fe5ce1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daichi Yamamoto <dev@dyama.net>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:25:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Support Zig 0.17.1 build system

Zig 0.17 removed custom build runners ("--build-runner"): "build.zig"
is now run by separate "configurer" process, which serializes resulting
configuration for "maker" process.

For 0.17+ releases, get path to that configuration with
"zig build --print-configuration-path", and pass it to new
"0.17.1.zig" program (run with "zig run") which reads it using
"std.Build.Configuration" and sends the same report as build runners.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
